WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.980
<b>Reinberg Estate, Garden</b>

00:03.470 --> 00:06.860
Anna, do you like me this way?

00:07.610 --> 00:08.610
Yes!

00:08.980 --> 00:10.680
I do, and so does everyone else.

00:11.320 --> 00:15.320
We all love our kindhearted 
Young Master Julius very much.

00:32.010 --> 00:36.720
Episode 20
Teachings of the Witch

01:47.380 --> 01:51.010
<b>Tower, 1st Floor, East End: Fields of Solitude</b>

01:58.930 --> 02:00.560
How many times does this make?

02:01.100 --> 02:03.160
You destroyed another guardian.

02:03.160 --> 02:05.480
You haven't made 
the slightest bit of progress!

02:05.480 --> 02:07.940
Just how much of my magical energy
do you plan on wasting?

02:07.940 --> 02:09.780
I-I'm sorry!

02:09.780 --> 02:13.500
<i>No matter how I try, the longest 
I can restrict my output is fifty minutes!</i>

02:13.500 --> 02:16.230
<i>After that, the magical energy dissipates.</i>

02:16.230 --> 02:21.980
<i>Worse, when I dispel Wis,
all my stamina drains from me at once!</i>

02:21.980 --> 02:24.500
<i>I never realized it had such a downside!</i>

02:24.500 --> 02:27.960
<i>At the rate I'm going,
 all of this is just a waste of time.</i>

02:28.230 --> 02:29.090
Again!

02:31.160 --> 02:33.220
What are you doing? Get in position!

02:33.620 --> 02:34.970
Julius!

02:34.970 --> 02:39.390
I think it'd be best if we learn more
 about Wis first after all.

02:39.390 --> 02:42.960
I mean, even I don't really 
understand what this power is.

02:44.060 --> 02:46.660
<i>I checked nearly every book
 in the academy library</i>

02:46.660 --> 02:49.000
<i>but couldn't find anything relevant.</i>

02:49.000 --> 02:51.840
<i>Professor Workner 
seemed to have an idea,</i>

02:51.840 --> 02:54.110
<i>but said he didn't know the specifics.</i>

02:55.090 --> 02:57.900
It'll take time, but maybe 
I should ask the high mages

02:57.900 --> 03:00.120
to let me look through 
the tower libraries.

03:00.120 --> 03:02.620
Or maybe I can find someone 
who knows something!

03:02.620 --> 03:04.910
I'm already doing all that!

03:05.220 --> 03:06.120
What?

03:06.760 --> 03:10.000
I've sent one clone to the libraries
 of the Upper Institute.

03:10.400 --> 03:12.690
Another is asking Professor Eliza to help

03:12.690 --> 03:17.580
find Finn from the People of the Light, 
who seemed to know something!

03:18.180 --> 03:20.490
You're remotely controlling Ars Weiss?

03:20.490 --> 03:22.260
Since when could you do that yourself?

03:22.260 --> 03:24.460
We're pressed for time right now!

03:24.460 --> 03:28.840
I have no choice but to commit to training
 and intel gathering simultaneously!

03:31.520 --> 03:36.900
Blast it. My head is all jumbled up from
seeing three perspectives at once.

03:36.900 --> 03:38.910
This is why I hate multitasking!

03:39.830 --> 03:42.450
Why would you do all of this for me?

03:43.790 --> 03:46.340
Out of calculated 
self-interest, of course!

03:46.340 --> 03:47.540
Get a clue already!

03:48.010 --> 03:52.040
As a mage from the Reinberg family, 
I will rise to the top without fail!

03:52.040 --> 03:54.640
I'm using you to that end! Nothing more!

03:54.640 --> 03:59.150
And nobles are always good for their word!

03:59.150 --> 04:00.180
That's all this is!

04:02.180 --> 04:05.830
<i>That's right. Julius kept his promise
after the Grand Magic Festival.</i>

04:05.830 --> 04:09.660
<i>Even to Master Donnan 
and the other dwarves.</i>

04:12.560 --> 04:15.950
Julius... you're really kind, aren't you?

04:16.550 --> 04:17.570
Huh?

04:18.020 --> 04:21.570
I think kindness takes different 
forms with different people.

04:22.290 --> 04:24.950
The kindness of Colette, 
who's always saving me,

04:24.950 --> 04:28.460
and the kindness of Professor Workner, 
who scolds me, are different.

04:28.840 --> 04:31.960
Sion has kindness in him, too.

04:32.830 --> 04:36.090
Even if it's just noblesse oblige,

04:36.090 --> 04:40.440
Julius, I think you're amazing and kind!

04:41.340 --> 04:44.850
<i>Young Master Julius, 
you're very kind, aren't you?</i>

04:46.920 --> 04:48.600
What are you saying all of a sudden?!

04:48.980 --> 04:50.600
You really are creepy, you know that?

04:51.560 --> 04:53.360
I'm going to rest a bit.

04:53.360 --> 04:56.360
Okay! I'm going to keep 
working a little longer!

04:56.990 --> 04:58.690
Thank you, Julius!

05:01.960 --> 05:04.120
<i>What's he mean, "kind"?</i>

05:04.700 --> 05:07.620
<i>Kindness doesn't matter.</i>

05:08.000 --> 05:10.870
<b>Lighsnow
Flurry Kitten</b>

05:09.470 --> 05:10.870
You're all right now.

05:17.460 --> 05:21.430
<b>Anna Eils</b>

05:18.570 --> 05:21.630
Young Master Julius, 
you're very kind, aren't you?

05:21.630 --> 05:23.220
Of course I am!

05:23.220 --> 05:26.730
Helping the weak is a noble's duty!

05:36.000 --> 05:39.150
Anna, do you like me this way?

05:39.880 --> 05:40.900
Yes!

05:41.270 --> 05:43.280
I do, and so does everyone else.

05:43.280 --> 05:47.470
We all love our kindhearted 
Young Master Julius very much.

05:52.550 --> 05:54.000
<i>Don't lie.</i>

05:55.630 --> 05:58.030
<i>It didn't matter how kind I was.</i>

05:58.030 --> 06:02.130
<i>I lost you in the end, didn't I?</i>

06:09.500 --> 06:12.020
<i>So I've cast aside kindness.</i>

06:12.760 --> 06:14.720
<i>Selfishness has better benefits, no?</i>

06:15.460 --> 06:19.290
<i>I'll show off my talents and 
use others to my advantage.</i>

06:19.290 --> 06:22.500
<i>I'll sneer at the weak and I'll gloat.</i>

06:23.490 --> 06:27.120
<b>Tower, 1st Floor: Residential Area</b>

06:23.650 --> 06:27.120
<i>Julius, I think you're amazing and kind!</i>

06:29.390 --> 06:32.910
<i>Don't look at me the same way 
Anna did and talk about kindness.</i>

06:33.550 --> 06:35.960
<i>I have no need for kindness.</i>

06:36.800 --> 06:41.840
<i>The Julius Reinberg who was kind 
and nothing more... I killed him long ago.</i>

06:47.680 --> 06:50.510
<b>Tower, 1st Floor, Floating Castle No. 1: Valny</b>

06:50.560 --> 06:53.520
<b>Kreutz's Laboratory</b>

06:50.930 --> 06:52.790
Such a meaningless struggle.

06:53.520 --> 06:57.180
Charles, contact our fellow colorless.

06:57.180 --> 06:58.020
Yes, sir!

06:58.020 --> 07:00.270
<b>Director of the Upper Institute 
& Head of the Colorless Faction
Kreutz Harlon</b>

07:06.910 --> 07:10.410
Blast it! Is this the dungeon
 or something?

07:13.260 --> 07:14.210
Frall!

07:18.640 --> 07:20.040
Who are you people?

07:20.400 --> 07:22.110
Mages of the Upper Institute?

07:22.110 --> 07:24.050
On orders from the higher-ups.

07:24.320 --> 07:29.300
We're to punish the miscreants
 running amok in our garden

07:24.320 --> 07:29.300
<b>Tony Harvey</b>

07:29.340 --> 07:32.310
<b>Mary Law</b>

07:29.340 --> 07:32.310
<b>Auron Cheek</b>

07:29.690 --> 07:32.310
and put a stop to your unsightly training!

07:32.910 --> 07:35.340
You mean to get in our way?

07:35.340 --> 07:38.560
All so we won't stand a chance 
in the next Bloom?!

07:38.560 --> 07:40.770
You're supposed to be 
members of the tower!

07:44.430 --> 07:46.210
You can't possibly understand!

07:46.210 --> 07:48.490
We've made it to the tower
but can't get anywhere!

07:48.490 --> 07:51.240
You know nothing 
of our humiliation as colorless!

07:52.610 --> 07:55.370
I refuse to remain 
a mere cog in the tower forever!

07:56.320 --> 07:58.370
Lord Kreutz promised us!

07:58.370 --> 08:02.880
If we crush you, he'll send letters of 
recommendation to every faction for us!

08:05.600 --> 08:07.940
<i>So this is the result of cruel
rivalry within the tower.</i>

08:08.300 --> 08:10.340
<i>In desperation to get out 
of the graveyard,</i>

08:10.340 --> 08:12.640
<i>these wands have abandoned 
even their pride!</i>

08:13.160 --> 08:15.640
<i>But even corrupted, 
they're still high mages.</i>

08:18.010 --> 08:23.110
<i>I've been overusing my guardians and 
Ars Weiss, so I don't have much magic left.</i>

08:23.490 --> 08:25.860
<i>Plus, they've got me outnumbered.</i>

08:26.750 --> 08:27.800
<i>In which case...</i>

08:29.660 --> 08:32.160
Tony, my senior by only a year...

08:32.550 --> 08:34.280
Mary on her high horse...

08:34.710 --> 08:37.410
And Auron, who was cocky 
despite being my underclassman.

08:37.990 --> 08:41.780
After developing new magic and 
ascending to the tower so quickly,

08:41.780 --> 08:45.420
it seems you've become complete failures,
haven't you, you former prodigies?!

08:45.420 --> 08:47.300
What a sorry sight!

08:47.300 --> 08:49.700
Shackled as tightly as can be 
by the Upper Institute...

08:49.700 --> 08:53.930
I'd rather die than end up
as fettered trash like you!

08:53.930 --> 08:56.680
You weren't scouted either! 
You're colorless, too!

08:57.890 --> 08:59.600
Are you blind?

09:00.230 --> 09:03.190
I am Julius Reinberg!

09:03.190 --> 09:07.290
I will use that magically incompetent 
no-talent and whoever else I need to!

09:07.290 --> 09:10.990
I will race up this tower and 
become Lady Elfaria's successor!

09:12.060 --> 09:13.270
And then...

09:16.370 --> 09:18.180
From the greatest heights of the tower,

09:18.180 --> 09:21.000
I will look down on everyone 
who abandoned me!

09:21.000 --> 09:24.000
To that end, 
I'll even use the Magia Vander!

09:24.000 --> 09:28.580
Though I'm sorry to say you lot
aren't even <i>worth</i> using!

09:28.580 --> 09:29.630
Julius!

09:29.630 --> 09:32.360
Even at school, I could never stand you!

09:32.360 --> 09:33.510
I'll kill you!

09:35.350 --> 09:38.270
<i>That's right. I'm not kind.</i>

09:38.700 --> 09:43.020
<i>Right now, these people in front of me 
who hate me are living proof of that.</i>

09:43.990 --> 09:45.720
<i>You see, Anna?</i>

09:45.720 --> 09:48.340
<i>I'm not kind anymore.</i>

09:56.860 --> 09:58.290
Are you all right, Julius?

09:58.550 --> 10:00.230
Sorry I took so long!

10:03.700 --> 10:05.890
Why are you...

10:05.890 --> 10:08.140
I was suddenly attacked by high mages,

10:08.140 --> 10:10.920
so I thought you might be in danger, too.
Kiki and I came looking!

10:12.910 --> 10:15.180
Why did you save me?

10:15.180 --> 10:16.120
Huh?

10:16.120 --> 10:19.780
Well, I mean, we saved each other a lot 
in the dungeon for the all-student praxis,

10:19.780 --> 10:22.180
and you're helping me 
 even now, so...

10:22.460 --> 10:25.940
Do you even realize how stupid I made 
you look at the Grand Magic Festival?

10:25.940 --> 10:30.620
I told you this is all just self-interest!
I'm only using you, yet you still...

10:30.940 --> 10:33.200
Are you daft?!

10:33.910 --> 10:35.270
Yeah, I am.

10:35.270 --> 10:38.460
When people are kind to me, 
I just can't help liking them.

10:38.460 --> 10:39.830
I'm a real fool.

10:40.120 --> 10:42.120
I do, and so does everyone else.

10:42.120 --> 10:47.020
We all love our kindhearted 
Young Master Julius very much.

10:48.290 --> 10:49.590
Phoo!

10:49.590 --> 10:53.000
Wh-Why'd you punch me?!

10:54.330 --> 10:55.470
I hate you!

10:55.470 --> 10:58.260
I positively despise you!

10:58.520 --> 11:00.580
What are they doing?

11:00.580 --> 11:03.480
It doesn't matter! 
Hurry up and crush them!

11:04.020 --> 11:05.460
Julius, stay back!

11:05.460 --> 11:07.100
Don't order me around!

11:08.770 --> 11:09.360
What?

11:13.410 --> 11:18.370
This isn't how we use magic. 
Didn't you learn that at the academy?

11:22.050 --> 11:23.520
Who are you?

11:24.410 --> 11:26.200
I am Cerridwen.

11:25.120 --> 11:29.000
<b>Cerridwen</b>

11:26.430 --> 11:29.000
For that lovely showcase
 of the springtime of youth...

11:29.290 --> 11:32.090
Allow me to become your teacher.

11:33.260 --> 11:34.650
<b>Chaos Kettle Wand</b>

11:33.300 --> 11:34.770
<b>Gouvion Broom</b>

11:34.670 --> 11:38.050
<b><u>Cerridwen</u>

Race: Rhizanth
Age: "Eternally 20," according to her
 Height: 175 cm
Birthday: 7th of Carnsmoon
Likes: Children who aim for the future
Dislikes: Adults who try to close off the future</b>

11:34.670 --> 11:38.050
<b>First Love: A very awkward, once dear friend
 who couldn't abandon their sweetness
Deepest Dungeon Floor Reached: 40th
Equipment: Chaos Kettle wand, Gouvion broom
Skills: Nearly every from all six elements other than light

The rest is a secret</b>

11:38.300 --> 11:39.550
<b>Lonedark Wand</b>

11:39.680 --> 11:43.060
<b><u>Charles Lauer</u>

Race: Rhizanth   Age: 22   Height: 173 cm
Birthday: 31st of Carnsmoon
Likes: Kreutz, artificing
Dislikes: Loud, angry voices; violence; hysteria
Someone He Likes: Monica Orphen

Deepest Dungeon Floor Reached: 28th
Equipment: Lonedark wand
Skills: Dark spells through the intermediate level</b>

11:39.680 --> 11:43.060
<b>A mage who serves as aide-de-camp to the colorless faction. 
As an artificer, he's skilled enough that even Kreutz 
acknowledges him as his right hand. However, 
at the same time, his timid personality often means he
gets caught up in the trouble around him. He's the one 
who works the hardest and suffers the most in the colorless faction.</b>

11:43.450 --> 11:45.500
I am Cerridwen.

11:45.500 --> 11:48.060
For that lovely showcase
 of the springtime of youth...

11:48.490 --> 11:51.050
Allow me to become your teacher.

11:51.960 --> 11:53.550
Cerridwen?

11:53.550 --> 11:56.320
Hey, hang on. That name...

11:56.650 --> 12:00.420
Just like the watchers, she's one
 of the seven legends of the academy.

12:00.420 --> 12:04.030
Night after night, she abducts students 
and conducts experiments on them.

12:04.030 --> 12:05.380
The Witch of the Hammer!

12:06.290 --> 12:09.130
I don't do scary things like that.

12:09.130 --> 12:13.840
When I find students who interest me, 
I train and guide them. That's all.

12:14.270 --> 12:17.340
Just like the two of you here before me.

12:17.340 --> 12:21.470
Train and guide... us?

12:21.470 --> 12:22.420
Exactly!

12:22.420 --> 12:27.230
I don't think you know this, 
but I've been watching you two for <i>ages</i>.

12:27.690 --> 12:29.990
<i>She's been watching us?</i>

12:29.990 --> 12:32.440
<i>I've never once met this witch before.</i>

12:37.150 --> 12:39.310
We can discuss the details later.

12:39.310 --> 12:40.610
First, let us go elsewhere.

12:41.140 --> 12:44.120
If we stay here, others from
 the Upper Institute will find us.

12:44.820 --> 12:47.870
For now, just play along and 
let me ensnare you, won't you?

12:51.080 --> 12:53.630
<b>Mercedes Caulis
The Wizard's Tower</b>

12:51.480 --> 12:57.130
Why didn't you bestow your blessing 
on Julius Reinberg, Lady Elfaria?

12:54.090 --> 12:57.130
<b>Elfaria's Private Chambers</b>

12:57.130 --> 12:59.890
When someone as talented 
as he is lies in obscurity,

12:57.800 --> 13:02.340
<b>Unearthing Agency Watcher
Iris Churchill</b>

12:59.890 --> 13:03.140
as a watcher, I cannot overlook that.

13:03.610 --> 13:08.360
But he said such lewd things like he was 
going to lay me bare and all that.

13:08.360 --> 13:11.510
Plus, he bullied Will so much.

13:11.510 --> 13:12.900
And...

13:12.900 --> 13:16.650
he revealed my dark past 
to the entire academy!

13:18.250 --> 13:21.040
So this is just a personal grudge?

13:21.040 --> 13:24.380
Besides, it was Will who actually 
revealed that, wasn't it?

13:24.380 --> 13:25.380
I don't care!

13:27.830 --> 13:29.500
Iris...

13:29.500 --> 13:33.540
What does Lord Aaron make of Will?

13:34.020 --> 13:37.220
He said, "Let things fall as they may."

13:37.550 --> 13:40.890
Lord Aaron differs 
from Headmistress Caldron.

13:40.890 --> 13:45.550
He's not as warm to the idea 
of a sword joining the wands.

13:46.000 --> 13:49.320
However, if the sword means 
to carve his own path,

13:49.320 --> 13:53.100
he will respect that will and strength.
 That seems to be his stance.

13:53.560 --> 13:55.620
<i>Will Serfort...</i>

13:55.620 --> 13:59.320
<i>With the advent of Wis, 
the tower is split on how to proceed.</i>

13:59.320 --> 14:02.500
<i>In the first place, what is Wis?</i>

14:02.500 --> 14:05.070
<i>I myself don't fully understand it.</i>

14:05.390 --> 14:07.920
<i>A power that could turn
 the whole world on its head...</i>

14:07.920 --> 14:09.830
<i>In every sense of the word,
 it is abnormal.</i>

14:10.420 --> 14:12.640
<i>While it's disrespectful 
toward Lady Elfaria,</i>

14:12.640 --> 14:15.400
<i>I haven't yet decided how 
we should regard him either.</i>

14:15.710 --> 14:19.300
In any case, should Will's treatment
 become questionable,

14:19.300 --> 14:23.590
as a watcher, I will take guardianship 
of him, so please don't worry!

14:23.590 --> 14:26.430
You really shouldn't sleeptalk 
unless you're asleep, you know?

14:26.430 --> 14:27.720
You thieving little cat.

14:31.150 --> 14:36.480
<i>Thanks to that young man... 
the tower may truly fracture.</i>

14:36.480 --> 14:38.820
And we're here!

14:36.860 --> 14:40.480
<b>Somewhere on the Tower's 1st Floor</b>

14:45.060 --> 14:47.740
Welcome to the Witch's Manor.

14:50.290 --> 14:54.000
<b>Clairie's House
Secret Base for Single Witches</b>

14:50.360 --> 14:52.140
Sit wherever you'd like.

15:10.550 --> 15:12.640
Now, let's have some dinner!

15:13.280 --> 15:15.020
I made it all myself!

15:15.270 --> 15:17.580
We'd never eat what
some suspicious witch has—

15:17.580 --> 15:19.370
Thank you for the meal!

15:19.370 --> 15:21.060
Don't eat that!

15:21.060 --> 15:23.850
Kiki says it's fine. Don't worry.

15:25.680 --> 15:27.220
First things first...

15:27.220 --> 15:28.910
What even is this place?

15:29.750 --> 15:33.910
A hideout Clairie secretly built 
on the first floor.

15:34.350 --> 15:36.530
I'm using it with her blessing.

15:37.230 --> 15:38.920
This is Miss Clairie's place?

15:38.920 --> 15:41.920
That's right! 
She is my apprentice, after all.

15:41.920 --> 15:44.090
She is?

15:44.090 --> 15:46.680
Although, somehow, 
that totally makes sense.

15:46.680 --> 15:50.550
So she got that carefree attitude 
of hers from her mentor?

15:50.550 --> 15:55.230
Now, what are you plotting
to use this blockhead for?

15:56.220 --> 16:01.310
Julius, she saved both of us, 
and she says she's Miss Clairie's mentor.

16:02.000 --> 16:04.820
You need to learn to be 
more wary of people!

16:05.150 --> 16:09.070
She could be an assassin from the
 Upper Institute just putting on a show!

16:09.070 --> 16:10.990
And even if she isn't,

16:10.990 --> 16:14.330
a mage perfecting their craft 
never gives away their services for free!

16:14.710 --> 16:16.800
Just like the seven legends say,

16:16.800 --> 16:19.580
she could mean to use us as test subjects!

16:20.670 --> 16:23.550
Well, this certainly is a problem.

16:23.550 --> 16:27.840
Being cautious is a sign 
of a brilliant mage, but...

16:27.840 --> 16:29.470
Well, in that case...

16:34.670 --> 16:37.260
<i>A massive magic barrage?!</i>

16:37.260 --> 16:40.380
<i>She cast all that instantly
and with no incantations?!</i>

16:40.380 --> 16:41.980
<i>I didn't see her trigger any of it!</i>

16:42.420 --> 16:45.100
<i>Bolts of every element besides light...</i>

16:45.100 --> 16:48.490
<i>This woman is a Multos! 
She has multiple affinities!</i>

16:48.950 --> 16:54.990
If I were so inclined, I could 
dominate you in two seconds flat.

16:56.590 --> 17:00.620
This isn't proof of anything, 
but I hope it convinces you.

17:01.270 --> 17:06.500
If I had any ill intent, you'd have been
 gobbled up by this scary witch already.

17:09.880 --> 17:11.990
First, tell us what you're really up to.

17:11.990 --> 17:13.890
What's your game?

17:14.180 --> 17:17.890
Otherwise, I will never allow you 
to be this fool's mentor!

17:18.310 --> 17:19.770
Julius!

17:19.770 --> 17:23.650
Don't get the wrong idea! 
I'm the only one who gets to use you!

17:23.650 --> 17:26.120
I won't let someone else 
just swoop in and steal you!

17:26.120 --> 17:27.650
That's what I'm objecting to!

17:27.650 --> 17:31.650
I am not kind! Not in any way, 
shape, or form! Do you hear me?!

17:32.870 --> 17:34.280
Understood.

17:35.910 --> 17:37.160
Firstly...

17:37.630 --> 17:40.540
I know just the tiniest bit about Wis.

17:42.820 --> 17:45.580
I may be able to help you.

17:45.580 --> 17:48.800
That is the first reason 
I appeared before you.

17:49.090 --> 17:50.550
As for the second reason...

17:50.870 --> 17:52.840
That'd be the Upper Institute's fault.

17:52.840 --> 17:55.550
Their methods aren't the best, but...

17:55.550 --> 17:59.600
Will, there are powers there 
 trying to fence you in.

17:59.600 --> 18:00.860
The Upper Institute?

18:01.700 --> 18:02.560
Don't tell me...

18:03.060 --> 18:04.440
You mean that man?

18:06.010 --> 18:08.560
Will Serfort has disappeared?

18:08.560 --> 18:11.620
Yes, along with Julius Reinberg.

18:11.620 --> 18:14.700
According to the reports, 
it appears someone intervened.

18:14.700 --> 18:17.080
Begin an exhaustive search!

18:17.080 --> 18:21.240
There are no magical signs 
that anyone has left the first floor.

18:21.240 --> 18:23.330
They must be hiding here somewhere.

18:23.670 --> 18:26.580
<b>Aide to the Director of the Upper Institute 
Charles Lauer</b>

18:24.330 --> 18:26.580
May I ask something?

18:27.350 --> 18:33.040
Why would you risk Lady Elfaria's 
animosity just to entrap Will Serfort?

18:33.040 --> 18:37.600
Why would I hand such fine material 
over to those battle-crazed factions?

18:37.600 --> 18:43.560
Wis should be used 
efficiently and effectively.

18:46.280 --> 18:49.070
Just like this mage slayer.

18:49.610 --> 18:55.110
I don't know what organization created it, 
but its potency is magnificent.

18:55.110 --> 18:58.870
Even monsters of low intelligence can 
wield it, and they can be mass-produced.

18:58.870 --> 19:02.690
Such a weapon could transform even 
inept mages into valuable soldiers.

19:03.040 --> 19:05.930
<i>This</i> is where our aspirations should lie.

19:06.750 --> 19:10.420
Power comes from numbers. 
Even efficiency is dictated by numbers.

19:11.320 --> 19:13.630
With just the five strongest blades,

19:13.630 --> 19:16.430
the Celestial Host was nigh unstoppable.

19:16.820 --> 19:21.930
We shouldn't be seeking lone superlatives,
but rather a standardized supremacy.

19:22.500 --> 19:26.080
Turning Wis into a power 
that anyone can use...

19:26.080 --> 19:29.060
That is, undoubtedly, the challenge 
before the Upper Institute.

19:30.270 --> 19:32.320
And to solve it, first...

19:32.590 --> 19:34.760
Will Serfort's body...

19:36.400 --> 19:38.520
must be dissected!

19:43.520 --> 19:47.490
<i>None of the factions, not even 
the Magia Vander, know about this.</i>

19:47.490 --> 19:49.440
<i>Lord Kreutz's hidden side...</i>

19:50.310 --> 19:52.170
<i>The Mad Dissector!</i>

19:52.170 --> 19:55.170
<i>If Lady Elfaria ever found out,</i>

19:55.170 --> 19:57.270
<i>the Upper Institute would be done for!</i>

20:09.300 --> 20:10.190
Charles.

20:11.420 --> 20:15.660
Tell the factions that we will soon have 
countermeasures against the mage slayers.

20:15.660 --> 20:17.700
I understand the principle behind them.

20:18.350 --> 20:22.260
The next thing I will unravel is Wis.

20:25.160 --> 20:26.770
The truth is...

20:28.030 --> 20:33.650
I wanted to watch over you as you
went on your own strength,

20:36.210 --> 20:38.350
but I can't sit idly by any longer.

20:39.000 --> 20:42.470
I absolutely do not want you 
to become a test subject.

20:43.110 --> 20:46.980
That's why I've decided
to lend you my aid.

20:47.350 --> 20:50.730
Plus, darling little Elfaria begged me to.

20:51.710 --> 20:52.980
Elfie did?

20:52.980 --> 20:57.740
And that's all about me. What you choose
 to make of it is up to you.

21:01.690 --> 21:02.870
Julius.

21:03.990 --> 21:05.870
I want to trust her.

21:08.360 --> 21:10.580
<i>I feel like she isn't lying.</i>

21:10.580 --> 21:12.880
<i>And, it's strange, but...</i>

21:13.250 --> 21:16.930
<i>I feel like I've known her 
for a long time.</i>

21:20.630 --> 21:22.640
Do whatever you want.

21:22.940 --> 21:24.390
Julius!

21:24.390 --> 21:27.260
Go ahead and switch to someone
 who you can make more use of!

21:27.260 --> 21:30.620
That's the whole reason I offered 
to help you in the first place!

21:30.620 --> 21:34.220
Wait, switch?! That's not what I'm doing!

21:34.220 --> 21:37.800
I'm really sorry! 
Thank you for being kind to me!

21:35.690 --> 21:38.030
<i>They get along so well now.</i>

21:37.800 --> 21:44.030
I told you! I'm not kind! 
I'm being efficient! That's all!

21:38.300 --> 21:40.510
<i>I think they'll make a wonderful party.</i>

21:44.030 --> 21:45.030
All right then!

21:45.560 --> 21:47.100
Now that we've reached an agreement,

21:47.100 --> 21:51.290
Professor Cerridwen will give you 
some training to power you up!

21:51.830 --> 21:54.130
Now, I know it's sudden, but...

21:55.310 --> 21:56.630
take off your clothes.

21:59.050 --> 22:00.260
Beg pardon?

23:28.050 --> 23:31.010
<b>Wistoria: Wand and Sword</b>

23:36.720 --> 23:39.630
Next time on <i>Wistoria: Wand and Sword</i>,

23:39.630 --> 23:42.900
episode 21, "The Page to Be Turned."

23:40.480 --> 23:45.990
Episode 21
The Page to Be Turned
